00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.440
Pardon me!

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.160
<i>Together—!</i>

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.160
I don't understand this at all.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.120
<i>And so, here we have—</i>

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:20.960
<i>What's that supposed to mean?!</i>

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.750
<i>Which is that at the time of the crime, the town was—</i>

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:25.630
Everything's so boring.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.430
Is this some kind of ritual?

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.050
<i>We are terribly sorry.</i>

00:07:34.050 --> 00:07:36.510
<i>We were not aware that you had business with Sir Sasaki.</i>

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:37.890
<i>Don't mention it.</i>

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.100
<i>May I ask how you know Sir Sasaki?</i>

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:43.900
<i>We faced each other once.</i>

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:48.570
<i>We were perfectly matched, and so we called it a draw.</i>

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:48.650
So boring.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:52.200
<i>I am here in all seriousness today to challenge him to a duel.</i>

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.260
Let's do it.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.760
We're back!

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.840
Huh? Where's Izo?

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:21.810
Seriously?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:24.140
<i>I will take your life!</i>

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:33.780
He didn't say anything about going after the pilot.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.320
Excuse me, please.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.870
There we go.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.290
Want one?

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.670
Uh, sure...

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:49.090
<i>The train will be arriving shortly at Platform One.</i>

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.920
Hurry! The next train will leave without us!

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.260
It gets rejected each time.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:01.220
Array, how did you get through so quickly?

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:04.230
I used this! The Chairman gave it to me.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:05.810
The Foundation is paying for all expenses.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:10.110
So why didn't you get me a ticket?

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.820
Sorry... This is for my use exclusively.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:16.360
Then why didn't you use that to buy some new clothes?

00:09:17.530 --> 00:09:19.740
And my grandson tells me:

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.040
"Grandma, you're wrong."

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:26.500
Imagine being lectured by a grandchild at my age.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:29.250
How about another tangerine?

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.630
Thank you.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:33.550
And my grandson tells me

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:35.420
that he's bringing home his girlfriend next time.

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:39.090
<i>If only I had my Ovid, I wouldn't have to put up with this.</i>

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:39.090
I got so nervous, as if it was happening to me!

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.850
Ouch.

00:09:44.350 --> 00:09:46.440
Madoka is late.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:48.900
She's probably busy gathering supplies.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:58.070
She doesn't show it, but she's definitely sad about Midori being locked away.

00:09:58.070 --> 00:09:59.320
You're right.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:02.370
The bond between the Vox and its pilot is very strong.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:03.080
Ouch...

00:10:03.870 --> 00:10:06.540
I wonder if it's like being pulled apart from a friend?

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:08.210
A close friend at that.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.210
Ouch.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.880
What are you doing?

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.050
Where is Izo?

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:25.020
He must be out looking for the Vox pilot.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.270
Where is Kyouno Madoka?

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.730
P-Please let me go.

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.780
I said, where is she?

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.610
Kamo Hurls...

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.570
Kamo Hurls, you said?

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:40.820
All right.

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:45.580
Madoka's house is straight down this street...

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:55.380
The smell of the ocean breeze is the same here as in De Metrio.

00:11:02.220 --> 00:11:03.260
Welcome.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.280
One Sangayaki Burger, please.

00:11:17.280 --> 00:11:18.070
Sure.

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:18.690
Huh?!

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:28.250
I'm coming!

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.330
I'm coming!

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:44.640
"Kamo Hurls?" That punk sent me on a wild goose chase.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.220
86th Annual Kamo Girls' Oraga Cultural Festival

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.220
86th Annual Kamo Girls' Oraga Cultural Festival

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.220
86th Annual Kamo Girls' Oraga Cultural Festival

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.190
What should we do?

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:55.650
<i>Is this where I have to perform that ritual?</i>

00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:59.440
Pardon me!

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:02.610
A pervert!

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:07.990
Thank you for the food.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:09.660
It was delicious.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:13.920
What's this supposed to be?

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:16.630
As you can see, a black card.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:21.420
Do we look like a shop that takes credit cards?

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.380
What? You don't?

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:27.050
What'll I do? I don't have any cash.

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.930
You can't dine and dash!

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:33.060
If you don't have money, you'll have to work it off.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.030
Thank you so much!

00:12:40.030 --> 00:12:42.070
How can I ever repay you?

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:45.660
How about hurrying home and giving him a warm bath?

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:48.780
Thank you so much!

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:52.700
I'm glad he's safe!

00:12:52.700 --> 00:12:53.790
Success!

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:00.800
Here.

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.590
Oh, thanks! And you folded it too!

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.800
Do you always wear a swimsuit?

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:09.600
I just happened to be wearing one today.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:15.230
Say, haven't we met before?

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:18.060
No, I don't think so.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:21.780
Your voice sounds so familiar.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.530
Oh well, never mind.

00:13:23.860 --> 00:13:27.450
I have to go shopping. So, bye!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.290
That's right...

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:37.000
I should have asked her where I could find Kyouno Madoka.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:40.250
Here you go.

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:45.010
I'm a guy, you know...

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.010
It doesn't matter.{/a/ in a nutshell}

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:49.800
We are terribly sorry!

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.350
Our students behaved very rudely towards you.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:59.190
We didn't know you were here to see Madoka...

00:13:59.190 --> 00:14:02.480
I'm sorry, but may I ask how you know her?

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.650
I knew it. It's that ritual.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.780
Well... it's...

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.200
We were perfectly matched!

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:19.250
Did you hear that?

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.460
They found themselves to be a perfect match!

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:28.550
Ahem... Now then, Miss Igarashi...

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:31.390
Yes, Captain?

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.600
We must get more details!

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.480
You girls...

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.850
Our Madoka radar...

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.980
... has detected a powerful signal!

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.320
<i>I don't quite get it,</i>

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:50.780
<i>but it looks like the ritual worked.</i>

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:53.030
So that's the kind of relationship you have?

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.620
Yes, I'm here in all seriousness...

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.290
How did the rest go?

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:01.790
You're serious about her?

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:02.670
Yes.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:03.790
I'm rooting for you!

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:08.220
So where is Kyouno Madoka now?

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:10.630
Madoka is at the Jersey Club...

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:13.350
Who is this Georgy Cub?

00:15:13.350 --> 00:15:16.260
Is Cub a man or woman?!

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:20.890
Is he a real airhead?

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:23.360
Madoka's boyfriend is so funny.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:25.860
A jersey is...

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:27.860
What is "jersey"?

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:30.860
That thing you're wearing.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:34.370
This?

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:36.830
And Cub?

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:38.660
Who are you calling chubby?

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:40.580
He didn't say that.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:44.750
It's a club where you do stuff while wearing a jersey.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.420
I don't understand what you're saying.

00:15:47.420 --> 00:15:50.670
We don't really understand what we're talking about either.

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:55.220
It all started when Madoka's mother...

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:58.310
... died in the ocean.

00:16:01.180 --> 00:16:05.610
Imagine, dying while trying to save someone from drowning.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:10.740
The incident left Madoka very depressed.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.490
And then she met Youko.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.100
<i>Doesn't this taste good?</i>

00:16:44.730 --> 00:16:46.350
<i>Want some, Madoka?</i>

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:50.070
<i>Cheer up.</i>

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.190
<i>That's right.</i>

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.700
<i>Madoka, wait!</i>

00:17:26.140 --> 00:17:27.350
After that incident,

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:30.270
Madoka recovered, more cheerful than ever.

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:33.110
She even started imitating Youko by wearing a jersey at all times.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.070
Ms. Machiko, too.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:36.490
That's right!

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:39.780
Ms. Machiko used to hang out with Youko.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.410
I remember now!

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:44.830
She kept insisting that she was just freelancing for the club, though.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:48.460
But the Jersey Club <i>are</i> freelancers, so I wonder what's up with that.

00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:54.510
Wait! I said wait!

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.300
Now I got—!

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.720
That's Madoka, the one you're looking for.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:09.270
You shouldn't climb up so high that you can't get down.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:10.810
Madoka!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:13.280
Your boyfriend is waiting.

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:14.360
Boyfriend?

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:16.820
Whose?

00:18:16.820 --> 00:18:19.030
Yours, of course!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.030
Huh?

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:22.080
I have a boyfriend?

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.420
Where is he?

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.590
He was just here.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:35.960
Maybe he got shy.

00:18:38.050 --> 00:18:40.050
My jersey!

00:18:49.060 --> 00:18:51.810
Thank you. Here's your paycheck.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:58.400
I deducted the cost for your Sangayaki Burger though.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:08.580
Did you find Izo?

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:11.540
What about me?

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.340
Where were you?

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.630
What's it to you?

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:21.840
You didn't try to do anything with Kyouno Madoka, did you?

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.350
I lost interest, that's all.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.480
What the hell are you doing?!

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.690
I must attend a ceremony,

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:39.490
so please pardon my appearance.

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.490
I need to inform you.

00:19:43.950 --> 00:19:46.830
The Vox Retrieval Force that was dispatched

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:48.700
will be a bit late.

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:50.500
<i>Is there a problem?</i>

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.750
Nothing to be concerned about.

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:55.710
Our field commander fell for the enemy's diversion

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.000
and is now forced to take a detour.

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:00.590
<i>Then I'm to assume Kiss will arrive here</i>

00:20:00.590 --> 00:20:02.630
<i>before the Vox Retrieval Force?</i>

00:20:05.010 --> 00:20:09.100
I must attend the ceremony for the conquest of Sensimiria.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:11.850
<i>So they finally fell.</i>

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:14.400
It doesn't mean we won against De Metrio.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:16.310
I wish you luck.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:25.320
You should have just stayed quiet, back in the sanctuary of U-Go...

00:20:28.200 --> 00:20:29.620
Villagiulio.

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:42.470
Oh man.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:45.050
Hey, you're late.

00:20:45.050 --> 00:20:46.510
What are you doing?

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:47.430
Playing a game.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:49.060
That's not what he's talking about that.

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:52.930
It's a game played by the people of this planet. It's fun!

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:57.730
The main retrieval force from Le Garite is coming.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:00.110
We'll destroy the Voxes before that happens.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:03.150
You're going to fight them?

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.200
That's right.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:07.620
The chairman has no intention of handing over the Voxes to Le Garite.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.030
Can you be sure of that?

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.120
Yes.

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.620
She doesn't intend to give them to us either.

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:14.000
Yeah, but...

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:18.290
And no matter how much the guys on this planet resist,

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:21.130
Dizelmine won't give a damn.

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.050
He will take them back without fail.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:26.800
Just what do you want from us?

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.470
Nothing.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:32.600
I just don't want you guys to do anything to mess things up.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:37.150
But from now on, you're free to do as you please.

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:40.150
You can come with me or you can go.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:41.650
It's all up to you.

00:21:43.490 --> 00:21:44.650
I...

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:47.530
will destroy the Voxes.

